x86_64-windows  one guard cxx1 writes and clang does not: ?u@?$Box@H@@2HA$guard. A template's static member built dynamically is guarded by a weak flag beside the object where clang gives its construction a COMDAT function of its own, as template-static-data-member-ctor.nonames records; one guard per object, nothing links against it (h1, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-18)
